{
  "$comment": "Developer Harness V2 permission transition — the ONLY authority an owner-launched bypassPermissions session has. Protected policy file (docs/developer-harness-v2/**): a bypass session can never write it; changes need owner review. The engine ceiling (scripts/developer-harness-v2/bypass-authorization.mjs) bounds every entry: nothing here can authorize a forbidden action, a credential read, a policy or agent-configuration edit, a merge, production or customer-agent operations. See 14-v2-permission-transition.md.",
  "version": 1,
  "owner_decision": {
    "date": "2026-11-24",
    "by": "repository owner",
    "summary": "While Developer Harness V3 is being built, the owner launches development sessions with `claude --dangerously-skip-permissions` and does not administer routine tool permissions. Routine development and the D3.3 scope below proceed without prompts; everything outside them is denied."
  },
